  "modern": "Dass. Let AB, ED, (fig. 8) be the incident rays tending to F, a point beyond the centre C, and let DR be the reflected ray of the incident one ED. Then because the incident ray ED tend to a point beyond the centre, the reflected ray DR will proceed as from one on the contrary to, flopode 2 as as- related above under Drop, VII. Through D draw the perpendicular CD, and produce it to H. Thus will EDH and HDD be the angles of incidence and reflection, while being equal, their vertical ones of DF and CDR will be so to cases constantly the vertex of the triangle FDR and bisected by the line CD+ wherefore, RD is to DF, or (3 Elem d o) BD vanishing, RB is to DF as RC to CF; that is, the dilatance of the focus of the reflected rays is to that of the imaginary focus of the incident rays, as the dilatance the lower from the center is to the dilatance of the latter from the same. _@E.D._"
